Summary of LGPL v3 (Not Legal Advice)
================================================================================

The LGPL v3 allows:
- Free use of the library in any application (commercial or open-source)
- Dynamic linking without source code disclosure of the application
- Distribution of binaries using the library

The LGPL v3 requires:
- The library must remain under LGPL (can't relicense)
- Users must be able to replace the library with modified versions
- Modifications to the library itself must be released under LGPL
- License and copyright notices must be preserved
- Source code or object files must be available for relinking

For Qt specifically:
- Qt is used as a shared/dynamic library (DLL/SO)
- Application code can be proprietary/closed-source
- No need to disclose application source code
- Must allow users to swap Qt libraries

================================================================================
Obtaining the Full License Text
================================================================================

Option 1: Download from GNU
wget https://www.gnu.org/licenses/lgpl-3.0.txt

Option 2: From Qt Installation
Qt installations include the full LGPL v3 text in:
<qt-install-dir>/Licenses/LICENSE.LGPLv3

Option 3: From Qt Source
git clone https://code.qt.io/qt/qt5.git
# License files in qt5/LICENSE.*

